<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Subhi Barakat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1889–1939</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Subhi Barakat was a Syrian politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> who led the Syrian Federation created by the French mandate authorities in 1922. When the federation was replaced by the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in 1925, he became its head of state, but resigned in 1925 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-syrian-revolt">Great Syrian Revolt</a>. He later served as speaker of the Syrian parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/subhi-barakat.jpg" alt="Subhi Barakat" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sammy.aw · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Subhi_barkat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
